From 6f6fb14daddcb58f0e37e9d5bdad0c69ee1f906f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HFM <hfm@ocp>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 18:02:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH zephyr] subsys/pmci/mctp: add MCTP-over-I3C binding (DSP0233
 v1.0)

Add a new libmctp binding that transports MCTP frames over Zephyr's I3C
controller API. The Zephyr guest is the I3C primary controller; a peer
target signals a pending frame with an IBI carrying MDB = 0xAE, and the
controller drains the frame through a private I3C read. Outgoing packets
are written back with a private I3C write. An 8-bit PEC (SMBus CRC-8,
poly 0x07, seed 0x00) is appended to and verified on every frame.

The binding is opt-in via CONFIG_MCTP_I3C, requires I3C_CONTROLLER, and
selects I3C_USE_IBI. CONFIG_MCTP_I3C_MTU defaults to 69 B per DSP0233
v1.0 s6.1.

Instantiate with:

    static struct i3c_device_desc peer = { .bus = ..., .pid = ..., };
    MCTP_I3C_DT_DEFINE(mctp_i3c, DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(i3c0)), &peer);

Signed-off-by: HFM <hfm@ocp>
